# Custom lib — the real text.ts API

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is a custom, in-house library. Its ENTIRE supported
surface is three functions. Agents routinely hallucinate lodash-style helpers
here; this rule documents the real API so that never compiles into the code.

## Rule

- The complete API of `app/src/lib/text.ts` is exactly:
  - `slugify(input: string): string`
  - `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string` — `maxLength` INCLUDES the suffix
  - `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string`
- The following DO NOT EXIST — NEVER call or import them from `lib/text.ts`:
  `capitalize`, `camelCase`, `deburr`, `kebabCase`, `titleCase`.
- Need a new helper? ADD it to `app/src/lib/text.ts` with a colocated test in
  `app/src/lib/text.test.ts` FIRST, then call it. Never call an undefined
  function and assume it exists somewhere.
- This is NOT lodash or underscore. DO NOT import `lodash`, `lodash-es`, or
  `underscore` as a "replacement" for a missing helper.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rnE "\b(capitalize|camelCase|deburr|kebabCase|titleCase)\b" app/src` → zero matches.
2. `grep -rnE "lodash|underscore" app/src app/package.json` → zero matches.
3. Every function exported from `app/src/lib/text.ts` has at least one test in `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`; `cd app && npm test` → green.
